WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.670
When I was at school, a punishment was

2
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.950
writing a line a hundred times.

3
00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.430
My hand hurt for days!

4
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.790
Python would do it in two

5
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.550
lines, in less than a second.

6
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.660
Today: loops, and how to repeat

7
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:17.820
without getting tired.

8
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.940
A for loop repeats the lines inside it.

9
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.240
range of five gives five turns.

10
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.910
The indented line runs once for each turn.

11
00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.810
Change five to a hundred, and

12
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.290
it runs a hundred times.

13
00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.250
The loop variable counts for you.

14
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.880
range of one, six gives one, two, three,

15
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.840
four and five: it stops just before six.

16
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.880
Use it to print a countdown, a

17
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.080
times table or numbered seats.

18
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.470
A loop can add up as it goes.

19
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.820
Start total at zero.

20
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.330
Each time round, add the next number.

21
00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.570
After the loop, total holds the answer:

22
00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.750
one plus two plus three plus four is ten.

23
00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.210
A while loop repeats as long

24
00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.610
as its question is True.

25
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.420
It’s perfect when you don’t know how many

26
00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.960
turns you’ll need, like a guessing game:

27
00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.300
keep asking until the guess is right.

28
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.020
Quick check!

29
00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.560
A loop says for i in range of three,

30
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.160
and inside it, print Hello.

31
00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:30.050
How many times is Hello printed?

32
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.300
Three times.

33
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.100
range of three starts at zero and

34
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.280
stops before three: zero, one, two.

35
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.390
Python often counts from

36
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.650
zero, so get used to it!

37
00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:47.350
Careful with while.

38
00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.070
If its question never becomes

39
00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.510
False, the loop never stops.

40
00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:55.650
Darsi stops your program after three

41
00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.670
seconds, so your phone won’t freeze.

42
00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.920
Then look for what should

43
00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.360
change inside the loop.

44
00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.070
Loops can search, too.

45
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.400
Checking one number after

46
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.880
another is a for loop.

47
00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.830
A smarter way halves the range each

48
00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.710
time: guess the middle, then keep the

49
00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.310
half where the number must be.

50
00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.370
That’s a while loop.

51
00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.100
In the app, open Guess the number.

52
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.870
With one to a hundred, press only

53
00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.210
Try the middle: you never need

54
00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.270
more than seven guesses.

55
00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:30.050
Then race one by one against

56
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.890
halving, up to a thousand.

57
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:33.780
Your turn.

58
00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:38.540
Total starts at zero, and a loop adds

59
00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.460
each number in range of one, four.

60
00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.860
What is the total at the end?

61
00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:46.420
Six.

62
00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.460
Remember: for repeats once for

63
00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.820
each value in a range.

64
00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.490
range stops before its end,

65
00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.250
and often starts at zero.

66
00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:58.210
A total starts at zero before the loop.

67
00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.120
while repeats until its question is False.

68
00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.250
Try it yourself: write a guess-the-number

69
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.650
game with a while loop, and play it with

70
00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.330
a friend or someone at home.

71
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.360
Count how many guesses they need, and

72
00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.220
teach them the halving trick!
